{
  "info": {
    "name": "Simple Order Service",
    "description": "REST API collection for the Simple Order Service.\n\nFlow: run Auth > Register first (stores the JWT in {{token}}), then Products > Create Product (stores {{productId}}; its SKU is the KOPI-ARABIKA-1KG literal), then Orders > Create Order (stores {{orderId}}). List/Get/Cancel requests reuse those variables. Register and Login use the same account — the email is written directly in both request bodies (bene@example.com): run Register once before Login, and edit the email in those two bodies (e.g. add +timestamp) to run against a database that already has that account.\n\nResponse envelope: successes are {\"data\": ...} (list endpoints add a \"meta\" object); errors are {\"error\": {\"code\", \"message\", \"details\", \"request_id\"}}. The HTTP status code is authoritative, and every response echoes an X-Request-ID header. The scripts only capture the returned token/product/order identifiers into collection variables — there are no assertions, so re-runs never report failures (a 409 from Register for an already-registered email is expected). Saved response examples show exact payloads for success and error cases. Prices are integers in IDR.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:8080"
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "productId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "orderId",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Health",
      "item": [
